    </svg>
    <span>IANA America/Denver</span>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- INTRODUCTION -->
<section class="acdt-intro content-section" aria-labelledby="intro-heading">
  <h2 id="intro-heading" class="sr-only">About Greenwich Mean Time to Mountain Daylight Time Conversion</h2>
  <p>
    Welcome to our dedicated <strong>GMT to MDT Converter</strong>, built for tech professionals, enterprise software teams, aviation dispatchers, and outdoor enthusiasts coordinating across Greenwich Mean Time (UTC+0) and Mountain Daylight Time (UTC-6). MDT represents the summer daylight saving time zone for the Mountain Region of North America, running exactly 6 hours behind Greenwich Mean Time.
  </p>
  <p>
    Greenwich Mean Time (GMT) serves as the primary universal solar reference computed at the Royal Observatory in Greenwich, London. Unadjusted for seasonal daylight shifts, GMT acts as the global benchmark for cloud database telemetry, international flight coordination, financial timestamps, and cross-border API integrations.
  </p>
  <p>
    Mountain Daylight Time (MDT) is active from mid-March to early November across key North American commercial centers such as Denver, Salt Lake City, Calgary, Edmonton, Albuquerque, and Boise. Navigating the 6-hour difference requires careful coordination, particularly when scheduling cross-Atlantic business meetings or managing cloud infrastructure deployments.
  </p>
  <p>
    This page features interactive live clocks, a customizable conversion tool, an hourly 24-hour reference matrix, detailed meeting planning recommendations, and technical timezone database specifications.
  </p>
</section>

<!-- INTERACTIVE CONVERTER & HERO GRAPHIC -->
<section class="hero" id="converter-section" aria-labelledby="converter-tool-heading">
  <div class="hero-copy">
    <p class="eyebrow">Interactive Conversion Tool</p>
    <h2 id="converter-tool-heading">Convert GMT to Mountain Daylight Time</h2>
    <p>
      Select any GMT time to calculate the corresponding Mountain Daylight Time instantly. Our calculator automatically handles date shifts and relative offsets.
    </p>

    <div class="custom-svg-container" style="margin-top: 1.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--panel);">
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 600 240" width="100%" height="auto" style="display: block;">
        <rect width="600" height="240" fill="#0c354a" rx="8" />
        <path d="M0 40 H600 M0 80 H600 M0 120 H600 M0 160 H600 M0 200 H600" stroke="#12455d" stroke-width="1" />
        
        <!-- GMT Node -->
        <g transform="translate(150, 120)">
          <circle cx="0" cy="0" r="55" fill="#12455d" stroke="#2f6278" stroke-width="3"/>
          <text x="0" y="-10" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="18" fill="#f4fbff" text-anchor="middle">GMT</text>
          <text x="0" y="15" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#8fd7ff" text-anchor="middle">UTC+0</text>
          <text x="0" y="32" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#bdd2dc" text-anchor="middle">Greenwich Meridian</text>
        </g>
        <!-- Arrow + Offset -->
        <g transform="translate(300, 120)">
          <line x1="-50" y1="0" x2="50" y2="0" stroke="#36c7b5" stroke-width="3" stroke-dasharray="6,4"/>
          <polygon points="45,-6 55,0 45,6" fill="#36c7b5"/>
          <rect x="-45" y="-22" width="90" height="24" fill="#1b536e" rx="4"/>
          <text x="0" y="-6" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="12" fill="#36c7b5" text-anchor="middle">-6 Hours Behind</text>
        </g>
        <!-- MDT Node -->
        <g transform="translate(450, 120)">
          <circle cx="0" cy="0" r="55" fill="#12455d" stroke="#36c7b5" stroke-width="3"/>
          <text x="0" y="-10" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="18" fill="#f4fbff" text-anchor="middle">MDT</text>
          <text x="0" y="15" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#36c7b5" text-anchor="middle">UTC-6</text>
          <text x="0" y="32" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#bdd2dc" text-anchor="middle">Denver / Calgary</text>
        </g>
      </svg>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Converter intent="dynamic" t={t} context={context} />
</section>



<!-- TIME DIFFERENCE & CALCULATION METHODS -->
<section class="method-section content-section" id="calculation-methods" aria-labelledby="methods-heading">
  <h2 id="methods-heading">How to Calculate GMT to MDT Time Differences</h2>
  <p class="method-intro">
    Converting GMT to MDT requires subtracting 6 hours from the Greenwich timestamp. Because MDT is observed during North American summer daylight saving months, ensure your query date falls between mid-March and early November.
  </p>

  <div class="custom-svg-container" style="margin: 1.5rem 0; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--panel);">
    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 700 200" width="100%" height="auto" style="display: block;">
      <rect width="700" height="200" fill="#0c354a" rx="8" />
      <text x="350" y="30" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="15" fill="#8fd7ff" text-anchor="middle">GMT to MDT Timeline Shift (-6 Hours)</text>
      <!-- GMT Bar -->
      <rect x="50" y="65" width="600" height="34" fill="#12455d" rx="4"/>
      <text x="70" y="87" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#f4fbff">GMT: 02:00 PM</text>
      <text x="350" y="87" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#f4fbff">06:00 PM</text>
      <text x="600" y="87" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#f4fbff">10:00 PM</text>
      <!-- MDT Bar -->
      <rect x="50" y="125" width="600" height="34" fill="#1b536e" rx="4"/>
      <text x="70" y="147" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#36c7b5">MDT: 08:00 AM</text>
      <text x="350" y="147" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#36c7b5">12:00 PM (Noon)</text>
      <text x="600" y="147" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#36c7b5">04:00 PM</text>
    </svg>
  </div>

  <div class="method-grid">
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>1. The -6 Subtraction Rule</h3>
      <p>Subtract 6 hours from the GMT time. For instance, 3:00 PM GMT minus 6 hours = 9:00 AM MDT. If the result is negative, roll back into the previous calendar day.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>2. Transatlantic Gap Strategy</h3>
      <p>With a 6-hour gap, European afternoon hours align with North American morning hours, making 2:00 PM to 5:00 PM GMT the ideal meeting window.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>3. Seasonal Transition Rule</h3>
      <p>MDT operates at UTC-6 during summer. During winter, North America switches to Mountain Standard Time (MST, UTC-7), increasing the gap to 7 hours.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>4. Arizona Exception Awareness</h3>
      <p>Most of Arizona remains on MST (UTC-7) year-round and does not observe MDT. Always confirm specific city locations in Arizona.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- STEP BY STEP GUIDE -->
<section class="content-section" id="step-by-step-guide" aria-labelledby="step-heading">
  <h2 id="step-heading">Step-by-Step Guide for Converting GMT to MDT</h2>
  <div class="method-grid">
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>Step 1: Check Target Date Calendar</h3>
      <p>Confirm your event falls between the second Sunday of March and the first Sunday of November when MDT (UTC-6) is active.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>Step 2: Input Starting GMT Time</h3>
      <p>Select your starting Greenwich Mean Time (UTC+0) value using our interactive picker tool.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>Step 3: Subtract 6 Hours for MDT</h3>
      <p>Deduct 6 hours from the GMT clock. For example, 16:00 GMT becomes 10:00 AM MDT in Denver.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>Step 4: Check Previous Day Rollover</h3>
      <p>If GMT is early morning (e.g., 03:00 AM GMT), subtracting 6 hours lands at 9:00 PM MDT on the previous evening.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

